# THIRTY MINUTES ON THE HOME COAST (docs/ROADMAP.md, slice 1): the slice's proof,
# played from the title the way a player starts, with nothing given, no folk and
# no beats pre-landed. Each step of the slice extends it.
#
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=600 TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/home-coast.tour --scene=title --seed=1
#
# At a fixed frame rate: from step 3 on a machine's tells are waited for, and a
# loaded box's frames let them go by (the keeper's block, as reaper_plating's).
# It may down him on the way to its plate; that is the fight, and it costs him
# hours and a meal, which is why the goal after it is his hunger's until step 4
# stages the fight itself.
#
# 1a THE WAKE (48_wake): a new game starts him under the water in the shallows
# off the spawn beach, the black site in the sea behind him and Maren at the
# water's edge. 01 he breaks the surface; 02 he stands in the surf with his legs,
# from above; 03 the first sight of the Tether; 04 over the shoulder, looking to
# the shore and her.
await title 40
# New game heads the title's list when there is no save to continue; with one,
# continue would, and `await character` below fails rather than play a save.
tap use
await character 8
key move_up
key use
# The island is raised behind the title (UiTitle._raise_island): a new game
# pressed at once waits on the loading page for the rest of that raise.
await game 120
await waking 5
wait 0.4
shot 01-he-breaks-the-surface with waking,wake:staged
await woken 10
wait 1.0
shot 02-in-the-surf-from-above with woken,cast:maren
# 1b THE FIRST SIGHT (48_wake, 42_stage): a breath after he stands, the view
# turns once to the far horizon and up the Tether to the Foundry, and holds.
await staging:tether 6
wait 1.2
shot 03-the-first-sight with staging:tether,tether
wait 4.0
tap shoulder
await shoulder 20
wait 1.0
shot 04-in-the-surf-over-the-shoulder with woken,cast:maren,shoulder

# 2 MAREN'S ASK BECOMES THE GOAL (Guide._led, StoryContent.LEAD): he goes to her
# at the water's edge and talks, taking the first reply each time, as a player
# who just keeps talking does, until she gives his first lead; then the goal
# line is her lead in her words, and it points on to the crew's camp.
at cast:maren
await cast:maren 8
wait 0.6
press use
await talking 3
wait 0.4
shot 05-maren-at-the-water with talking,cast:maren
press use
wait 0.5
press use
wait 0.5
press use
wait 0.5
press use
await beat:marens_lead 3
wait 0.5
shot 06-her-lead with talking,beat:marens_lead
press use
wait 2.5
shot 07-the-goal-is-hers with beat:marens_lead

# 3 THE FIRE, THE CHARCOAL, THE PICK (Guide._led: her lead in her words, in the
# order the way in asks: a fire, charcoal, a haft, plate, a pick). Everything is
# taken by hand from the coast round the spawn, nothing given: five takes of
# driftwood (a fire's three, a haft's two, a batch of charcoal's four), two
# stones, and a plate turned out of a tip. From above, as the making is done: at
# eye level the meadow's grass stands round him and no tile of it is open ground.
coast calm
tap shoulder
wait 1.0
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took:driftwood 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took:driftwood 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took:driftwood 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took:driftwood 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took:driftwood 4
end
wait 0.2
shot 08-driftwood-off-the-strand
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:stone 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:stone 14
end
try 3
  near tip
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:scrap 20
end
wait 0.2
shot 09-a-plate-turned-out-of-the-tip
ground grass
mark fire
press use 0.1
await fire_asked 2
# The ask is a prompt on the glass; the second press answers it once it is up.
wait 0.6
press use 0.1
await made:fire 4
wait 0.5
shot 10-his-fire-laid with station:fire
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose charcoal
tap use
wait 0.3
choose haft
tap use
await made:haft 3
tap pause
wait 0.4
hour 11
await made:charcoal 4
wait 0.3
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose pick_made
tap use
wait 0.3
tap pause
wait 0.4
hour 12
await made:pick 4
wait 0.3
tap inventory
wait 0.6
shot 11-a-pick-of-his-own with app:inventory
tap inventory
wait 0.4

# 4 THE TIDE REAPER, NAMED (Guide.edge_line, StoryContent.EDGE, KEEPER_NAMED):
# Hob, who picks the tide past the point, names the yard and its keeper and says
# what bites it; then at the keeper the knife rings off its plate, and the goal
# is the steel edge in Hob's words.
at cast:hob
await cast:hob 8
wait 0.6
press use
await talking 3
wait 0.4
press use
wait 0.5
press use
wait 0.5
press use
await beat:reaper_named 3
wait 0.5
shot 12-hob-names-it with talking,beat:reaper_named
press use
wait 1.0
near keeper
wait 0.6
await sentinel 12
# A blow on its plate is all the ring asks for (tours/sentinels.tour's 03), and
# each try starts off its body, so a try that ends with him downed and carried
# off does not walk the rest of them from wherever he came round.
try 8
  near mob:sentinel.coast 5
  walkto plate 6
  tap swing
  await plating 4
end
wait 0.4
shot 13-the-knife-rings-off-it with plating

# 5 THE STEEL (Guide.edge_goal, StoryContent.EDGE): back at his fire the goal is
# the steel edge in Hob's words, then everything it asks, gathered: four charcoal,
# eight stones, a kiln at Low Scar, the knife tempered over a night there. Low
# Scar is the Reaper's region's other village, 205 tiles off Oyster Row, where
# he woke and was seen; a night away is when the plan comes for who saw him.
at mark:fire
wait 1.0
# Fed first, as a player would be: the ring cost him hours and a hungry body's
# goal is its hunger (Guide), not the steel.
# Berries off the bushes on the grass round his fire (mussels come only at low
# tide, and a tour cannot wait on the sea), one at a time and eaten by it, until
# his hunger no longer outranks the steel: a berry puts his last meal an hour and
# a half later, and how far past it the ring has left him is the fight's.
try 10
  near bush
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:berries 8
  at mark:fire
  wait 0.5
  press use 0.1
  wait 1.5
  await goal:kiln_stones 2
end
shot 14-the-goal-asks-for-steel with beat:reaper_named,goal:kiln_stones
# Four charcoal for the temper, from two batches: the pick took one of the first.
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took:driftwood 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took:driftwood 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took:driftwood 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took:driftwood 4
end
at mark:fire
wait 0.5
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose charcoal
tap use
wait 0.3
tap pause
wait 0.4
# Forty minutes on the fire, waited out: how late the ring has left the day is
# the fight's, and `hour` only moves within the day.
await made:charcoal 45
wait 0.5
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose charcoal
tap use
wait 0.3
tap pause
wait 0.4
await made:charcoal 45
wait 0.3
village 36
wait 1.5
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:stone 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:stone 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:stone 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:stone 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:stone 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:stone 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:stone 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:stone 14
end
ground grass
mark kiln
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose kiln
tap use
await station:kiln 20
# The making page stays open after a build; shut, so the frame is the kiln.
tap pause
wait 0.6
shot 15-a-kiln-at-low-scar with station:kiln
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose knife_cemented
tap use
wait 0.3
tap pause
wait 0.4
hour 20
village 36
wait 1.0
# A hungry body eats what it carries before it lies down (Survival._fallback):
# fed first, a press a mouthful. On seed 7 the presses meant for sleep ate
# berries ("berries - eat" under the hand) and he never lay down. Each press
# waits for the row to name it: seed 7's village 36 is a shift town whose
# street puts somebody in front of him most seconds, and the press is theirs.
try 8
  until hint:eat 4
  press use 0.1
  wait 0.4
  await fed 1
end
# Sleep is asked for: the first press asks, the second sleeps.
try 3
  until hint:sleep 4
  press use 0.1
  wait 0.4
  until hint:sleep 4
  press use 0.1
  await slept 6
end
at mark:kiln
wait 0.5
await made:knife_shear 10
wait 0.5
tap inventory
wait 0.6
shot 16-steel-in-his-hand with app:inventory
tap inventory
wait 0.4

# 6 WHO SAW HIM (48_raids, SnatchNight): while he was away at the Reaper and at
# Low Scar, the plan came in the small hours for somebody out of Oyster Row, and
# holds them at the Reaper's region's yard. Staged by name: the small hours it
# comes in are a seed's (SnatchNight.due), the night he slept at Low Scar on seed
# 1 and the night after on seed 7.
hour snatch
await taken 5
# At one of its housings, the yard in frame round him (its middle is its mast).
at rescue:yard_breaker
wait 1.0
await held_here 6
shot 17-the-yard-holding-somebody-from-oyster-row with works,works_lit,works_yard

# 7 ITS FALL, BY THE TIDE (44_sentinels, the FOUNDER way): it keeps the tide line
# and is far too heavy for the mud and water it works beside. Roused, it follows
# him off its own shore onto the mud beside its den, founders there
# (held 1.4 s), and the land takes it. Staged by the ground's name, and walked
# as a lure is: at it until it starts a bite at him, then a run for the flats
# with it behind him. Jumped onto the flats, he was gone from it behind the rise
# 9 tiles off, and it lost him and never came.
# Every try starts at its den: a try that ends with him downed and carried off
# would take the next one's walk from wherever he came round. He goes in from
# its flats and runs back the way he came (`near keeper_flats`, the nearest
# patch of them its move reaches from its den): stood off its den on the side
# he arrived from, terraces and the intake's fence stood between him and the
# water. The shallows run four tiles off its den (336 tiles of mud, wash and
# river inside its reach, seed 1; Sentinels.ways_closed holds every den to them).
try 6
  near keeper
  await sentinel 12
  near keeper_flats
  wait 1.0
  walkto mob 4 till:tell
  walkto ground:mud,water,river 6 run
  await sentinel_fallen 20
end
wait 1.0
shot 18-the-tide-takes-the-reaper with sentinel_fallen

# 7a TODO THE FORCE FIGHT (roadmap step 4, owed to the fight's builder): the
# Reaper taken apart with the steel knife through its openings. Measured with the
# scripted player (near mob, walkto plate, await tell 10, dodge, await
# sentinel_open 6, walkto part, swing), 30 passes before its body was gone: no
# tell at its plate 23 times, a tell but no opening 2, an opening and a swing 4.
# At that rate a force fall is some 200 passes; headless (test_fight, the hero
# placed every tick) it is 28 swings. Routed to fight as a balance finding.
echo todo: the force fight (7a)

# 7b TODO THE STARVE WAY (roadmap step 4, owed to fight/reaper-reachable): "The
# intake feeds it. Rob the intake." Robbing a plan work is Takes' kept `turn`, and
# a kept take spent sets SurvivalState.spent, never world.depleted; the keeper
# counts its feed off world.depleted (Sentinels.feeds_among), so a robbed intake
# fed it for ever and the way could not be won by a player. Ruled: robbing a
# keeper's feed depletes it in the world.
echo todo: the starve way (7b)

# 8 ITS YARD GOES DARK (34_works): the fall line, then some minutes on, the yard
# its keeper held puts its lights out for good.
near keeper_yard
await works_broken 30
wait 1.0
shot 19-its-yard-dark with works_broken,works_dark

# 9 THE RESCUE (45_taken): with the yard dark, whoever it held out of Oyster Row
# walks out of it.
await freed 30
wait 1.0
shot 20-somebody-from-oyster-row-walks-out-of-the-dark-yard with works_dark,freed

# 10 HOME AGAIN (35_folk, 45_taken): back at Oyster Row, where he woke and was
# seen, the village is whole: the plan holds nobody of it and one of its people
# has come back out of the yard. Read off the record, not walked 188 tiles home
# (a tour's walk has no path yet; ROADMAP tools track).
village 0
wait 2.0
await home_again 10
shot 21-oyster-row-with-its-own-home-again with home_again

# 11 WHAT HE OWES THE CREW (Guide._goal_of, LEAD.crew): the Reaper down and Oyster
# Row whole, the goal is the crew's iron again, said for the dark yard, never "go
# mine" out of nowhere. The day's fights have left him hungry, and hunger outranks
# any lead: berries off Oyster Row's bushes, two picked and eaten off the carry
# page at a time, until the goal is the crew's and stays so.
# He goes to bed peckish and wakes some 900 minutes past his last meal's reach,
# hungry until under 360 (Body). One berry a try wins back 67 minutes, which puts
# the need at the try cap; and the try that crosses the line can land a minute
# under it, so the goal is held through a settle before its frame.
try 10
  near bush
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:berries 8
  near bush
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took:berries 8
  tap inventory
  wait 0.5
  choose berries
  tap use
  wait 1.0
  choose berries
  tap use
  wait 0.4
  tap inventory
  wait 1.0
  await goal:crew 2
  wait 1.0
  await goal:crew 1
end
shot 22-fed-the-goal-is-the-crews-iron with goal:crew
